> Actually, leaseEndpointReconciler never deletes endpoints

is not about deleting the endpoint, is about deleting the IP address of the endpoint, the operations when deleting has to be always an Update to the Endpoint object

The doReconcile build the endpoint based on the existing leases in etcd.
If the apiserver is the last one, RemoveEndpoints first deletes the lease and calls doReconcile.
doReconcile doesn't update the Endpoints to indicate "there are no IPs", because of
```
 if len(masterIPs) == 0 { 
 	return fmt.Errorf("no master IPs were listed in storage, refusing to erase all endpoints for the kubernetes service") 
 } 
```
